            </creation>
            <history xml:id="history_ide8d14b2a">
               <p xml:id="idm63">Having returned to Copenhagen, Scheibe also began on translating plays. In 1769, the translation of <persName xml:id="idm64" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Peder Topp Wandall</persName>’s comedy ‘Stedmoderen’, the original of which had appeared two years earlier and staged at the theatre during the season 1767–68, was published together with plays by <persName xml:id="idm65" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Charlotta Dorothea Biehl</persName> (cf. SchW C4:008).</p>
            </history>
